164. u4 nu2-a u4 di du11-ga-a-ba
#tr.en: The day of the New Moon, the day of judgement,
>>Q002295 164 
165. a-da-ba sag-ki zalag an-na sig5 mu-un-zu-zu-ne
#tr.en: They introduced Adaba to a favourable An.
>>Q002295 165 
166. an#-e a-da-ba gesztu2 ku3-zu igi-du8 {gesz}gu?#-za?# / mu-un-na-an-[szum2?]
#tr.en: An gave Adaba, the intelligent and wise one, a seat as an audience gift.
>>Q002295 166 
167. an#-e ninda i3-gu7-e a-ra-ab-du11-ga szu nu-um-gid2-de3
#tr.en: An was eating bread, he offered it to him, he did not accept it.
>>Q002295 167 
168. a-nag a-ra-ab-du11-ga szu nu-ma-gid2-de3
#tr.en: He offered water to him, he he not accept it.
>>Q002295 168 
169. szu?# il2-la! a-ra-ab-du11-ga szu nu-ma-gid2#-de3#
#tr.en: He offered the raised hand to him, he did not accept it.
>>Q002295 169 
170. ir-da-ni a-ra-ab-du11-ga ugu-zu# he2-bi-sig
#tr.en: He offered perfume to him, he put it on himself.
>>Q002295 170 
171. an-ne2# gu7?# nag?# bi2-du11-du11 zu2 na-NE-NE
#tr.en: An said: "Eat, drink!" and laughed:
>>Q002295 171 
172. a-a [{d}]en#-ki musz2-bi sig7-ga-gin7 zi-mu un nu-me-/da-an-szum2
#tr.en: Father Enki of the green space prevented me from giving my breath to the people.
>>Q002295 172 
173. an-ne2 unken-na digir gal-gal-e-ne gu3 mu-un-na-de3
#tr.en: An called to the great gods in the assembly:
>>Q002295 173 
174. a-da-ba im-ulu3 pa na-asz me-hasz#
#tr.en: Adaba, why have you broken the wing of the South Wind?
>>Q002295 174 
175. digir gal-gal-e-ne# an-e inim mu-un-na-<ni>-ib-gi4#-[gi4]
#tr.en: The great gods responded to An:
>>Q002295 175 
176. im-ulu3 pa-a-bi bi-ib-si-sa2 ur5 mu-un-da#-/zi-ga
#tr.en: He will put the wing of the South Wind in order, then it will be able to rise.
>>Q002295 176 
177. {d}en-ki-ke4 sag-du nigin2-na-a-ba
#tr.en: As Enki turned (his) head,
>>Q002295 177 
178. a2-ga2 bi-lu-da me an-na-ke4 kur-ra e3-de3
#tr.en: The commands, ordinances, and powers of An emerged in the land.
>>Q002295 178 
179. {d}en-ki-ke4 im-ulu3 [(x x x)] gu3 mu-un-na-de3
#tr.en: Enki spoke ... to the South Wind:
>>Q002295 179 
180. ga2-nun im-ulu3 sza3-zu?# nu?-du10? esz TU nam ga-mu-/ni-ib-tar-re
#tr.en: Come, South Wind, your heart is not good ..., let me fix your destiny!
>>Q002295 180 
181. edin? lu2# bi? ki si-ga-ni ur5-gin7 he2-da-ab-be2
#tr.en: In the steppe, let this man in his quiet place speak thus:
>>Q002295 181 
182. lugal mu-sar-ra sag5-ga-zu2?# im-ulu3 KUSZ2 nu ba-du10 (su?-he?)
#tr.en: O king, your beneficent inscription ... the South Wind
>>Q002295 182 
183. ambar gal-gal?# ki nig2 dagal-la-bi-ta
#tr.en: From the great marshlands, the broad places,
>>Q002295 183 
184. u4 x [x x x x x] x HA A ur im-szi-gen-na
#tr.en: ... went ...
>>Q002295 184 
185. IM# [...] HA A ur2 ha-ga?#-dib-be2
#tr.en: ...
>>Q002295 185 
186. x HA x [...] x
#tr.en: ...
>>Q002295 186 
187. gig-simx(GIG)-ma su nam-lu2-ulu3 SU mu!-un#-x-x
#tr.en: The simmu-disease ... the bodies of mankind,
>>Q002295 187 
188. im-ulu3 a-ba-an-zi-zi su-mu-ra gesztu# he2-em-szi-gub-en
#tr.en: When the South-Wind rises, may it attend to my body!
>>Q002295 188 
189. nig2-la2-a ku3 {d}nin-i3-si-na-ke4 sza3-mu hug-ga2
#tr.en: The pure bandage of Ninisina, which soothes my heart,
>>Q002295 189 
190. nun gal a-a {d}en-ki za3-mi2
#tr.en: The great prince, the father Enki, be praised!
>>Q002295 190
